# publish(underBoundOfItsOwn, besideCounter, storedInto);
# -- end of source
# `i < n` says nothing of `list[i]`, so each read asked `i < length` besides. In front of the typed build the lesser of the bound and the length is taken (of the length less what stands beside the counter in the key), the head
# asks the counter against it, and the reads ask nothing. Where the lesser bound is reached the turn goes to the other build, which asks as before. A list that the turns store into is left as it was.
# RUN: walk f1 f2 f3 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = GetArrayLength
# CHECK: = Less {{*}}form=Integers
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: = GetArrayElement {{*}}level=Proven [keyIsIntegral, isInBounds, readsHoleAsNaN
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
